.TH "DOCUMENT.CREATEPROCESSINGINSTRUCTION" "3JS" "August 13, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
Document.createProcessingInstruction \- Document:
createProcessingInstruction() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]createProcessingInstruction()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]Document\f[R] interface creates a new
\f[CR]ProcessingInstruction\f[R] object and returns it.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
createProcessingInstruction(target, data)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]target\f[R]
A string containing the first part of the processing instruction (i.e.,
\f[CR]<?target \&... ?>\f[R])
.TP
\f[B]data\f[R]
A string containing any information the processing instruction should
carry, after the target.
The data can contain any character pattern, except that it can\(cqt
contain \f[CR]?>\f[R], since that closes the processing instruction.
.SS Return value
.IP \(bu 2
A \f[CR]ProcessingInstruction\f[R] node.
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]InvalidCharacterError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown if either of the following are true:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
The \f[CR]target\f[R] value is not a valid \c
.UR https://www.w3.org/TR/xml/#dt-name
XML name
.UE \c
; for example, it starts with a number, hyphen, or period, or contains
characters other than alphanumeric characters, underscores, hyphens, or
periods.
.IP \(bu 2
The \f[I]closing processing instruction sequence\f[R] (\f[CR]?>\f[R]) is
included as part of the \f[CR]data\f[R] value.
.RE
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \f[CR]createProcessingInstruction()\f[R] method creates a new
processing instruction.
The new node will usually be inserted into a document to accomplish a
task with it, using a method such as \f[CR]node.insertBefore\f[R].
.PP
Initially, \f[CR]ProcessingInstruction\f[R] nodes were only supported in
XML documents, not in HTML documents.
In non\-supporting browsers, a processing instruction will be
interpreted as a comment and represented as a \f[CR]Comment\f[R] object
in the DOM tree.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic usage
This example creates an \f[CR]<xml\-stylesheet>\f[R] processing
instruction and adds it to the top of an example XML document.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] doc = \f[B]new\f[R] DOMParser().parseFromString(\(dq<foo />\(dq, \(dqapplication/xml\(dq);
\f[B]const\f[R] pi = doc.createProcessingInstruction(
  \(dqxml\-stylesheet\(dq,
  \(aqhref=\(dqmycss.css\(dq\(aq,
);

doc.insertBefore(pi, doc.firstChild);

console.log(\f[B]new\f[R] XMLSerializer().serializeToString(doc));
\f[I]// Displays: <?xml\-stylesheet href=\(dqmycss.css\(dq type=\(dqtext/css\(dq?><foo/>\f[R]
.EE
